// @@@ The index of the first occurrence of the specified element in the ordered set is not -1. For all indices i where 0 <= i < the index, the element at this position in the set is null and the specified object is not null, or the element at this position is not null and is not equal to the specified object.

--------------------
// @@@ The index of the first occurrence of the specified element in the ordered set is not -1, for all indices before it, the element at that index in the set is null or not equal to the specified object.

--------------------
// @@@ For any object that is added to the set, the index of the first occurrence of this object in the set is not -1. From the first occurrence to the index of the object in the set, all elements are either null and the object is not null, or they are not null and not equal to the object.

